.TH RUNE 1 "2026" "Rune" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rune \- fast, GPU-accelerated, full-featured IDE and terminal multiplexer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rune
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ file ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Rune
is a keyboard-driven IDE that combines code editing, terminals, CLI
tools, language intelligence, debugging and AI agents in one
multi-workspace environment. The GUI is GPU-rendered and needs an X11
and OpenGL capable display; \fB\-\-tui\fR and \fB\-\-headless\fR load no
graphical library and run on a host that has none installed.
.PP
Any files named on the command line are opened in the initial
workspace.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIfile\fR
Use \fIfile\fR to configure Rune. Defaults to \fBconfig.yaml\fR inside
the data directory.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-datadir " " \fIdir\fR
Set the data directory. Defaults to \fB~/.rune\fR.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-fps
Render the frame rate in GUI mode.
.TP
.BR \-G ", " \-\-gui
Run Rune in manual GUI mode.
.TP
.BR \-\-tui
Run Rune in TUI mode.
.TP
.BR \-\-headless
Run Rune as a headless network node for other Rune instances to connect.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print version information and exit.
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-workspace " " \fIuri\fR
Set the initial workspace to open, in the format
.IR [scheme:][//[userinfo@]host][/]path .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.rune
Default data directory holding configuration, state and installed
extensions.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/rune.app/share/zdot
Z shell startup files used to bootstrap Rune's integrated terminals.
.SH SEE ALSO
Full documentation is available at
.UR https://docs.rune.build
.UE .
